/strong> there are several challenges that must be addressed to ensure the sector&#8217;s continued success. Some of the most pressing challenges include:\u00a0<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-fe0a424 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"fe0a424\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-7327551\" data-id=\"7327551\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-67143bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"67143bd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><strong>1. Infrastructure:<\/strong> Canada&#8217;s vast geography and harsh climate can pose challenges for last mile delivery companies, particularly in rural or remote areas. Companies must invest in infrastructure and technology to ensure that deliveries can be made efficiently and reliably.<\/p><p><strong>2. Labor Shortages:<\/strong> The logistics industry in Canada is facing a labor shortage, with an aging workforce and a lack of skilled workers. This can make it difficult for last mile delivery companies to recruit and retain the talent they need to meet the demands of modern consumers.<\/p><p><strong>3. Sustainability:<\/strong> The growth of last mile delivery has raised concerns about its impact on the environment, particularly with respect to emissions from delivery vehicles. <strong>Last mile delivery companies in Canada<\/strong> must prioritize 